{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/MCP Network Observability Boundary.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/MCP Network Observability Boundary.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mcp network observability boundary mcp network observability boundary","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/MCP Network Observability Boundary.md","fileName":"MCP Network Observability Boundary.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"MCP Network Observability Boundary","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Network Monitoring and Remediation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Network Monitoring and Remediation","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/MCP Network Observability Boundary.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/MCP Network Observability Boundary.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mcp network observability boundary mcp network observability boundary","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/MCP Network Observability Boundary.md","fileName":"MCP Network Observability Boundary.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"MCP Network Observability Boundary","heading":"MCP Network Observability Boundary","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An MCP network observability boundary exposes named monitoring resources and analysis tools through a consistent protocol. A client can discover a health resource, a performance-trend resource, or a capacity tool without receiving unrestricted credentials to the underlying monitoring platform.\n\nThe server remains responsible for authentication, input validation, data retrieval, and side-effect policy. MCP standardizes access but does not make telemetry trustworthy or a change safe. Read-only resources should be separated from remediation tools so the risk and authorization of each capability remain visible.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Network Monitoring and Remediation","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/MCP Network Observability Boundary.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/MCP Network Observability Boundary.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mcp network observability boundary mcp network observability boundary","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/MCP Network Observability Boundary.md","fileName":"MCP Network Observability Boundary.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"MCP Network Observability Boundary","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[ainetworkingcookbook.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Network Monitoring and Remediation","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}